==English==

===Etymology===
The phrase dates back to 1910 (US).

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-bum's rush.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[bum]][['s]] [[rush]]|es}}

# {{lb|en|chiefly|North America|slang|idiomatic}} Forcible [[eject]]ion of someone, such as a [[bum]] ([[hobo]]), from an establishment.
#Idiomatic: To be hurried out of a social situation, brushed off.

